     "description": "Searches OpenAlex, arXiv and PubMed for published papers and preprints, outside the User's Documents. Set kind to \"drug_labels\" to search openFDA and DailyMed for drug labels (give a drug name). Set kind to \"clinical_trials\" to search ClinicalTrials.gov for clinical trials (give a condition, a drug or an NCT number). Set kind to \"us_law\" to search eCFR for US federal regulations (give key words), or to look up a citation: a CFR section or part (\"17 CFR 240.10b-5\", \"17 CFR Part 243\", \"17 CFR 240.10b-5 as of 2019-06-30\" for an earlier version) or a US Code section (\"42 U.S.C. 1983\", looked up at GovInfo when the User has added its key). Call it only when the User asks to find papers, articles, studies, drug labels, clinical trials, regulations, statutes or other published sources (for example \"find papers since 2021 on …\"), not to answer from the User's Documents. Write the query as the key words of the topic (a title, a DOI or an arXiv ID also works), in the language the field publishes in, usually English."
